    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0438" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg426"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.61/2022: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-04T13:00:00+03:00">June 4, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>596. The British Ambassador on three occasions has asked me whether I had
                    received any instructions from my Government relative to the taking of action
                    jointly with him in regard to the Polish situation. <pb facs="0439" n="427"
                        xml:id="pg427"/> He indicated that he had been informed that I would receive
                    such instructions and appeared disturbed at my reply in the negative.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Standley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
